From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: refuse interlaced MPEG-4 VOLs which can
 contain B-VOPs

The engine wraps the vertical field motion vectors of interlaced B-VOPs
to half their range, so their jobs fail. That only happens once
decoding has started, and userspace had to guess from the stream that
it should decode it in software.

Refuse interlaced VOLs without V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_LOW_DELAY in the
control check instead, so that userspace finds out when it tries the
VOL before decoding. The job time check stays for B-VOPs behind a wrong
low_delay flag. The engine has no low_delay setting (the vendor decoder
reads the syntax element and never uses it), so nothing is programmed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
index ad6103319..a518ca91a 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -201,6 +201,18 @@ static int cedrus_try_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 		if (vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_DATA_PARTITIONED)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * The engine wraps the vertical field motion vectors of
+		 * interlaced B-VOPs to half their range, and their jobs fail
+		 * (cedrus_mpeg4.c). Refuse interlaced VOLs which can contain
+		 * B-VOPs here already, so that userspace finds out when it
+		 * tries the VOL. The flag only gates this check: the engine
+		 * has no low_delay setting.
+		 */
+		if ((vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_INTERLACED) &&
+		    !(vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_LOW_DELAY))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		/*
 		 * In interlaced quarter sample VOLs, the engine derives the
 		 * chroma vectors of field predictions with another rounding
